Few notes for the C version of the code

* maintain file division started in 
  C++/src/TEOBResumS*.cpp
  
  Files TEOBResumSHlm.cpp and TEOBResumSWaveform.cpp can be merger in 
  TEOBResumSWavelm.cpp	  

  check also against the division in src_Sebastiano

* compute and store all the possible parameters at the very beginning

*  avoid things like 

   for (int i=grid_length; i--;)
    {
        switch (i)
        {
            case 0:
	    ...
            default:
	    ...

   where possible: loop on the default deal with the few cases separately.

* try to take adavatnge of auto-vectorization in e.g. multipolar loop.

  Simple rules
  - allocate aligned memory
  - avoid conditional inside loops


  Loops should look like:

   for (int k=kmin; k<kmax; ++k)
    {
    hlm[k] = hNetwlm[k] * fact[k] * Tlm[k];
    }

   and not

   for (int k=kmin; kmax; ++k)
    {
       if(a=1)
            hlm = hNetwlm[k] * fact[k] * Tlm[k];
    	else
            hlm = hNetwlm[k] * fact[k] * Tlm[k];

	... other operations on hlm other conditionals ...
    
     }

* use structure of arrays and not array of structures !

* use pointers to functions (set at the begining) to minimize
  conditional statements

* Ideally all the main functions should have similar syntax, e.g.

  instead of

  void hlmNewt(
    gsl_complex hlmNewt[], /** OUTPUT Dimension: 35*/
    const double r,
    const double Omega,
    const double phi,
    const double nu,
    bool tidal_flag){

  we might want something like

  int hlmNewt(
    params, // this could be even a global ...
    const double r, // input
    const double Omega,
    const double phi,
    const double nu,
    gsl_complex hlmNewt[] // output 
    ){

  with the functions returning errors

* Q: how about complex types? 
